### 2. The Filter Animations (Snap Fix)

**The Problem:**
You are using standard React rendering (`map`) for your lists. When `filteredUniversities` changes, React effectively destroys the old tree and builds a new one. Elements snap into place instantly.

**The Solution:**
Use Reanimated's `Layout` prop. This automatically animates items to their new positions when the list order changes or items are removed.

1. **Import Layout animations:**
```tsx
import Animated, { FadeIn, FadeOut, LinearTransition } from "react-native-reanimated";

```


2. **Wrap your card items:**
In `renderCardsForTab`, wrap every card in an `Animated.View`.

```tsx
// Example for Universities
if (tabKey === "universities") {
  return filteredUniversities.map((university, index) => (
    <Animated.View 
      key={university.id}
      layout={LinearTransition.springify().damping(14)} // Smooth reordering
      entering={FadeIn.duration(300)}                   // Fade in on filter match
      exiting={FadeOut.duration(200)}                   // Fade out on filter mismatch
    >
      <CardUniversity
         // ... props
      />
    </Animated.View>
  ));
}

```

*Apply this wrapper to the Faculty and Program maps as well.* This will make the list items smoothly shuffle around when you apply a filter, rather than snapping.

